  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Cosmic Opening and the First Draft",
  "paragraphs": [
   "John doesn’t start with a manger or a baby. He goes all the way back to before the universe even existed.",
   "\"In the absolute beginning was the Word. The Word was with God, and the Word was God. He was there before anything was created. Through him, literally everything was made. He brought life and light into the dark world, and the darkness could not stop it.\"",
   "There was a man named John, sent by God to be the ultimate hype man for the Light. He came to point everyone in the right direction—to show them who to look at and who to believe. John wasn't the Light himself; he was just there to shine the spotlight on it. The real Light—the one that lights up every single person on the planet—was coming into the world.",
   "John kept pointing at Jesus and shouting, \"This is the One I was telling you about! He comes after me, but he ranks way ahead of me—because he was here before I even existed. We are all living off his endless generosity—gift after gift after gift. Moses gave us the basics, the Law. But this over-the-top grace and truth, this endless knowing and understanding of God, all came through Jesus the Messiah. No one has ever seen God—not even a glimpse. But this one-of-a-kind Son, who is right at the Father's heart, has made him totally clear to us.\"",
   "He was right here in the world he made, and the world didn't even notice him. He came to his own people, and they shut the door on him. But everyone who welcomed him—everyone who believed he was who he claimed to be—he gave the ultimate upgrade: the right to become God's actual children. Not born because of blood or human effort or anyone's decision, but born by God himself.",
   "Then John drops the ultimate plot twist: The Word became actual flesh and blood and moved into our neighborhood. That \"Word\" was Jesus.",
   "The guys sent to question him were from the Pharisee party, and they had their own question: \"If you're not the Messiah, not Elijah, and not the Prophet—then why are you baptizing?!\" John answered, \"I only baptize with water. But standing right here among you is someone you don't even recognize. He comes after me, but he's not second place to me—I'm not even worthy to hold his coat for him.\" (All of this went down in Bethany, on the other side of the Jordan River, where John was baptizing).",
   "§The Hype Man Points Him Out",
   "John the Baptist was out in the desert baptizing people. The religious leaders sent a squad from Jerusalem to interrogate him: \"Who are you? Are you the Messiah? Elijah? A prophet?\"",
   "John the Baptist said, \"No, no, and no. I'm just the hype man shouting in the desert to get the road ready for the Lord.\"",
   "The very next day, John the Baptist saw Jesus walking toward him. John pointed right at him and yelled to the crowd: \"Look! The Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the entire world! This is the guy I was talking about. I saw the Holy Spirit come down on him like a dove. He is the Son of God!\"",
   "§Drafting the First Guys",
   "The next day, two of John the Baptist’s followers (Andrew and one of his buddies) heard him hype up Jesus again, so they just started following Jesus down the road. Jesus turned around: \"What do you guys want?\"",
   "They were awkward. \"Uh... Rabbi, where are you staying?\"",
   "Jesus smiled. \"Come and see.\" They hung out with him the rest of the day.",
   "Andrew was so excited he immediately ran to find his tough brother, Simon. \"We found the Messiah!\" Andrew brought him to Jesus.",
   "Jesus took one look at Simon and said, \"You are Simon. From now on, your name is Cephas (Peter, which means 'The Rock').\"",
   "The next day, Jesus found a guy named Philip and told him, \"Follow me.\"",
   "Philip immediately ran to find his buddy Nathanael. \"We found the guy Moses and the prophets wrote about! It's Jesus from Nazareth!\"",
   "Nathanael threw some massive shade: \"Nazareth? Can anything good even come out of that nowhere town?\"",
   "Philip said, \"Come and see.\"",
   "As Nathanael walked up, Jesus said, \"Look, a true Israelite with zero fake in him!\"",
   "Nathanael was suspicious. \"How do you know me?\"",
   "Jesus dropped a casual flex: \"Before Philip even called you, when you were sitting all by yourself under that fig tree miles away... I saw you.\"",
   "Nathanael’s jaw dropped. \"Rabbi! You are the Son of God! You are the King of Israel!\"",
   "Jesus said, \"You believe just because I said I saw you under a tree? Buckle up, man. You are going to see heaven ripped open and angels going up and down on the Son of Man.\""
  ],
