  "chapter": 4,
  "title": "The Woman at the Well and the Long-Distance Miracle",
  "paragraphs": [
   "Jesus had to travel from Judea to Galilee. The standard route went completely around the region of Samaria because Jews and Samaritans absolutely hated each other. They were bitter, racist rivals who wouldn't even use the same cups.",
   "But Jesus purposely walked right straight through the middle of enemy territory.",
   "He sat down by an ancient well in the middle of the day, exhausted. A Samaritan woman came out to draw water.",
   "Jesus casually asked her, \"Will you give me a drink?\"",
   "She was shocked. \"You're a Jewish guy, and I'm a Samaritan woman. Why are you even talking to me?\"",
   "Jesus said, \"If you knew who you were talking to, you would have asked me, and I would have given you living water. Anyone who drinks from this well will get thirsty again. But whoever drinks the water I give them will never thirst. It will become a spring of eternal life inside them.\"",
   "She said, \"Sir, give me this water so I don't have to keep hauling buckets out here.\"",
   "Jesus tested her: \"Go call your husband and come back.\"",
   "She looked down. \"I don't have a husband.\"",
   "Jesus read her entire life like an open book: \"You're right. You've had five husbands, and the guy you're sleeping with right now isn't your husband.\"",
   "She stepped back, stunned. \"Sir, I can see you're a prophet.\" She tried to change the subject to a religious argument about where people should worship.",
   "Jesus shut down the argument: \"It's not about the location anymore. True worshippers worship the Father in Spirit and in truth.\"",
   "The woman said, \"Well, I know the Messiah is coming eventually. He'll explain everything.\"",
   "Jesus looked right at her: \"I, the one speaking to you—I am he.\"",
   "She completely forgot her water jar, sprinted back into town, and yelled to everyone, \"Come see a guy who told me everything I ever did! Could this be the Messiah?!\"",
   "Just then his disciples came back from town with the food—and their jaws hit the floor. They were completely shocked to find him talking with that kind of woman. Nobody dared to say what they were all thinking, but their faces gave it all away.",
   "After two days, Jesus left and headed for Galilee. (Jesus himself had said that a prophet gets zero respect in his own hometown.) But these Galileans had been up in Jerusalem for the festival and had seen everything he did there—so they welcomed him and were eager to see him do it again.",
   "Meanwhile the disciples kept urging him, \"Rabbi, eat something!\" But Jesus said, \"I have food to eat that you know nothing about. The food that keeps me going is doing the will of the One who sent me and finishing the work he started.\" They looked at each other: \"Did somebody bring him food?\" Jesus went on: \"Look around—you'd say it's about four months until harvest, right? Well, I'm telling you, open your eyes and look at what's right in front of you. These Samaritan fields are already ripe. It's harvest time! The harvester is already getting his wages and gathering crops for eternal life, so the planter and the harvester can celebrate together. Here's the deal: I sent you to harvest a field you never worked in. Other people did all the hard labor, and you get to walk in and enjoy the results.\"",
   "Because of her testimony, the whole Samaritan town came out, and Jesus stayed with them for two days. Massive numbers of \"enemies\" believed in him.",
   "§The Long-Distance Flex",
   "Jesus left and went back to Cana in Galilee. A powerful royal official tracked him down and begged Jesus to come to Capernaum (about 20 miles away) to heal his son, who was on his deathbed.",
   "Jesus looked at the desperate dad and simply said, \"Go. Your son will live.\"",
   "The official took him at his word and started the long walk home. On the road, his servants ran up to meet him: \"Your boy is alive and completely recovered!\"",
   "The dad asked exactly what time the fever broke. The servants said, \"Yesterday at 1:00 PM.\" It was the exact second Jesus had spoken the words. The official and his entire household believed. That was the second miracle Jesus did after coming from Judea back to Galilee."
  ],
