  "chapter": 5,
  "title": "The Pool of Bethesda and the Boss Claim",
  "paragraphs": [
   "Jesus went back to Jerusalem for a festival. Near the Sheep Gate, there was a pool called Bethesda surrounded by massive covered colonnades. It was packed with blind, crippled, and paralyzed people who believed the water had magical healing properties if it got stirred up.",
   "Jesus walked through the crowd and saw a guy who had been an invalid, paralyzed on his mat, for 38 straight years.",
   "Jesus walked right up to him and asked, \"Do you want to get well?\"",
   "The guy made excuses. \"Sir, I have no one to help me into the pool when the water is stirred. Someone else always beats me to it.\"",
   "Jesus didn't offer to help him into the water. He just gave an order: \"Get up! Pick up your mat and walk.\"",
   "Instantly, the 38-year paralysis vanished. The guy grabbed his mat and walked away.",
   "§The Sabbath Trap and the God Claim",
   "But there was a catch: it was the Sabbath.",
   "The religious police saw the guy carrying his mat and threw a fit: \"It is illegal for you to carry your mat on the Sabbath! You're breaking the rules!\"",
   "The guy panicked. \"The man who healed me told me to pick it up!\"",
   "They demanded, \"Who told you to do that?!\" But the guy didn't even know Jesus's name because Jesus had slipped away into the crowd.",
   "Later, Jesus found the guy in the Temple and said, \"Look, you are well now. Stop sinning, or something worse may happen to you.\" The guy immediately ran and informed the Jewish leaders that it was Jesus who healed him.",
   "The leaders tracked Jesus down and started aggressively interrogating him for breaking their Sabbath rules.",
   "Jesus didn't back down. In fact, he doubled down with a claim that made them want to murder him: \"My Father is always at his work to this very day, and I too am working.\"",
   "The leaders absolutely lost their minds. Not only was he breaking the Sabbath, but he was calling God his own personal Father, literally making himself equal with God.",
   "They tried to kill him right there, but Jesus dropped a massive, unbreakable speech about his authority:",
   "\"I'll give it to you straight: the Son can do nothing by himself; he can only do what he sees his Father doing. The Father loves the Son and shows him everything.",
   "The Father judges no one, but has handed all ultimate judgment over to the Son, so that everyone will honor the Son exactly as they honor the Father. If you don't honor me, you don't honor God.",
   "Jesus kept going: \"Just like the Father raises the dead and gives them life, the Son gives life to anyone he chooses. And listen carefully—anyone who hears my word and trusts the One who sent me already has eternal life; they've crossed over from death into life without waiting for judgment day. The time is coming—and it's already here—when everyone dead and buried will hear the voice of the Son of God and come alive. Those who lived the right way will walk out into a resurrection of Life; those who lived the wrong way will walk out into a resurrection of Judgment.\"",
   "Jesus kept going: \"I can't do a single thing on my own. I listen, then I decide—and that's why my decisions are always right. I'm not trying to do my own thing; I'm here to do the will of the One who sent me. John was like a blazing torch, and for a while you loved basking in his light. But I have proof way bigger than John: the actual work the Father gave me to finish. These miracles prove the Father sent me. And the Father himself has backed me up—but you totally missed it. You've never heard his voice or seen his face, and his message isn't inside you, because you refuse to take his Messenger seriously.\"",
   "\"Here's the thing—I'm not interested in your applause or crowd approval. I know you guys. I know that God's love isn't even on your agenda. I came with the full authority of my Father, and you reject me—yet if some random guy showed up with his own credentials, you'd welcome him with open arms! How are you ever going to get anywhere with God when all you do is compete for position with each other and ignore the One standing right in front of you? And don't think I'm the one who will accuse you before the Father. Moses—the guy you put all your stock in—is your accuser. If you actually believed what Moses wrote, you'd believe me, because he wrote about me. But if you won't even believe his words, how are you going to believe mine?\"",
   "A time is coming, and has now come, when the dead will hear the voice of the Son of God, and those who hear will live. I have the authority to grant life.",
   "You diligently study the Scriptures because you think you have eternal life in them. But those very Scriptures point straight to me, and you refuse to come to me to get actual life! Don't worry, I won't accuse you before the Father. Moses will accuse you. Because if you actually believed Moses, you would believe me, because Moses wrote about me.\""
  ],
