  "chapter": 7,
  "title": "Undercover at the Festival",
  "paragraphs": [
   "The Jewish Festival of Tabernacles (a massive, week-long camping festival in Jerusalem) was coming up. Jesus's own brothers were mocking him: \"Why don't you go to Judea and show off your miracles? You can't be a public figure if you're hiding out here.\" (Even his own brothers didn't believe in him yet). Jesus told them, \"My time hasn't come yet. You guys go. I'm staying.\"",
   "But after they left, Jesus went to the festival in Jerusalem completely undercover. The entire city was buzzing about him. Half the crowd was whispering, \"He's a good guy.\" The other half was saying, \"No way, he's a scammer.\" But nobody talked too loud because everyone was terrified of the religious mafia.",
   "Halfway through the festival, Jesus walked right into the Temple courtyard and started teaching openly. The leaders were mind-blown. \"How does this guy know so much without any official theological degrees?\" Jesus answered: \"My teaching isn't mine. It comes straight from the God who sent me. If anyone actually wants to do God's will, they will realize my teaching is legit. You guys are trying to kill me because I healed a guy's whole body on the Sabbath. Stop judging by appearances and make a right judgment!\"",
   "The crowd was confused. \"Wait, isn't this the guy they are trying to assassinate? He's speaking publicly, and they aren't arresting him. Do the bosses actually think he's the Messiah?\" Jesus yelled out, \"You know me, and you know where I am from. But I am not here on my own authority. The one who sent me is true. You don't know him, but I do, because I came directly from him.\"",
   "The leaders were so furious they sent the Temple SWAT team to arrest him.",
   "\"I'm only going to be with you for a little while longer,\" Jesus fired back. \"Then I'm going back to the One who sent me. You are going to look for me, but you won't find me—and where I'm going, you cannot come.\" The leaders huddled up, totally confused. \"Where could he possibly go that we can't find him? Is he going to travel out and teach the Greeks? What is he even talking about—'you will look for me, but you won't find me,' and 'where I'm going, you cannot come'?\"",
   "The crowd split wide open over him. Some said, \"This has to be the Prophet!\" Others said, \"He is the Messiah!\" But others pushed back: \"Hold on—the Messiah doesn't come from Galilee, does he? Don't the Scriptures say the Messiah comes from David's family line, from Bethlehem, David's village?\" The crowd was totally divided. Some even wanted to arrest him on the spot, but nobody laid a hand on him.",
   "The Water Flex On the very last and greatest day of the festival, Jesus stood up and shouted to the massive crowd: \"Let anyone who is thirsty come to me and drink! Whoever believes in me, rivers of living water will flow from within them.\" (He was talking about the Holy Spirit, which hadn't been given yet).",
   "The Temple guards who were sent to arrest him came back to the chief priests empty-handed. \"Why didn't you bring him in?!\" the priests demanded. The tough guards were completely hypnotized: \"No one has ever spoken like this man.\" The Pharisees sneered. \"Did you get fooled too? Do you see any of the leaders believing in him? Only this crowd, who does not know the Law, believes him.\" Nicodemus (the guy who met Jesus at night) tried to defend him: \"Doesn't our law require a fair hearing before we condemn a guy?\" They mocked him. \"Are you from Galilee too? Look into it—no prophet comes out of Galilee.\""
  ],
